# The boot logo's picture and its two copper lists (47 KB of chip RAM) are freed once the
# game's copper list is showing, behind the black screen before the title's colours (SPEC 11,
# "The logo's memory"): nothing shows the logo again (no attract page, no credits, not the card,
# the hall of fame or a game over). They were held for the whole game; world 1 now plays with
# that much more chip, and the worlds after it start from there.
# - the marker: once, and the harness's frame count goes on (no dropped frame: the long frame
#   of the OS trip is a skipped one for the meter)
# - the guard: after the marker no `AGK mem` line shows less than 149 KB free (measured on the
#   a500, the profile with the least chip: 151 KB; the game's floor is 96 in tests/memory.agk,
#   64 in the squeeze test, and stays: this is the headroom the next worlds count on)
wait-serial "AGK t0" 1000
expect-serial "AGK splash freed"
expect-no-serial "AGK splash freed[\s\S]*AGK splash freed"
press fire 2
wait 125
press up 30
press left 170
wait 60
press down 70
expect-serial "landed x=2334"
wait 60
expect-no-serial "ERR|missing"
expect-no-serial "AGK splash freed[\s\S]*AGK mem chip=([0-9]|[0-9][0-9]|1[0-3][0-9]|14[0-8]) "
expect-no-dropped-frames
expect-min-chip-free 96
